      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cancer-related Fatigue (CrF) is a common disease that occurs in connection with oncological disease, characterised by feelings of fatigue and lack of energy and even after successful primary treatment of the underlying disease as an independent event in impairment of the health and quality of life as well as the ability to work can lead to vocational disability. There are indications that the affected persons suffer more from CrF than from pain."},
